# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Root .env — template. Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is gitignored.
#
# This file is committed and must NEVER hold a real value.
#
# Two secrets belong at the repo root, each read by one part of the migration
# tooling. The Sanity token lives in studio/.env instead, not here — the two
# loaders read different directories and are not interchangeable.
#
# THE WORKER'S SECRETS ARE NOT HERE. PRIVATE_PAGE_PASSWORD and
# PRIVATE_SESSION_SECRET go in `.dev.vars` locally and in `wrangler secret put`
# everywhere else; see .dev.vars.example. Different mechanism, different reader,
# and putting them here would not reach the Worker.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Webflow site API token. Read by migration-scripts/webflow/pull.mjs
# (`npm run wf:pull`) and by nothing else.
#
# Where: Webflow -> site Settings -> Apps & Integrations -> API access
#        -> generate a SITE token.
# Scope: read is sufficient. `wf:pull` only reads; nothing here writes to
#        Webflow, and a write-scoped token is a liability for no benefit.
WEBFLOW_API_TOKEN=

# Webflow's PER-PAGE password, for the pages that have one.
#
# Read by `npm run extract:private` and `npm run verify:private`, and by
# nothing else. Both trade it for a `wf_auth_page` cookie on
# `webflow.staging` — the only host that still serves the Webflow originals now
# that `webflow.source` is this site.
#
# This is WEBFLOW'S password, which is a separate thing from the one our own
# gate checks (PRIVATE_PAGE_PASSWORD, in .dev.vars). They may well be set to
# the same string so visitors notice nothing, and they are still two
# independent values: this one stops mattering when the Webflow project is
# deleted.
#
# Needed only to re-port a protected page. Normal builds do not read it.
WEBFLOW_PAGE_PASSWORD=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT SECRETS, AND NORMALLY ABSENT — read this before setting either.
#
# These are OVERRIDES, not configuration. The real values live in
# project.jsonc. migration-scripts/guard-production-deploy.mjs scans the shell
# plus .env, .env.local, .env.production and .env.production.local, and BLOCKS
# the deploy if any of them holds a non-production dataset.
#
# So leave both unset. Set one only deliberately and temporarily, to point
# local work at a non-production dataset — and expect `npm run deploy` to
# refuse until you remove it again.
#
# Consume these with `||`, never `??`. This file ships keys with no value,
# which load as an EMPTY STRING, and `??` only substitutes for null/undefined —
# so `SANITY_DATASET=` resolves to '' and every query in the build dies with
# "`dataset` must be provided".
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# SANITY_DATASET=
# SANITY_PROJECT_ID=
